From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serialize station persistence with native topology departures

The native controller crashed writing address4 in update_list's memcpy after
get_sta returned null. Station persistence chose a database update before the
lookup, without sharing the topology-notification mutex. A station can depart
during the database call; the metrics iterator also retains raw station pointers.

Protect association/departure/metrics persistence and map iteration with the
existing recursive topology mutex, releasing it before other tables and
publication. An absent direct update is ignored, never reinserted as a ghost.
This complements0193 without adding an ASan requirement or a new lock order.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
@@ -4808,6 +4808,7 @@
         }
     } 
 
+    std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> station_lock(g_network_topology_mutex);
     if (dm->db_cfg_type_is_set(db_cfg_type_sta_list_update)) {
         sta = static_cast<dm_sta_t *> (hash_map_get_first(dm->m_sta_assoc_map));
         while (sta != NULL) {
@@ -4899,6 +4900,8 @@
 		dm->reset_db_cfg_type(db_cfg_type_sta_metrics_update);
     }
 
+    station_lock.unlock();
+
     if (dm->db_cfg_type_is_set(db_cfg_type_network_ssid_list_update)) {
         for (i = 0; i < dm->get_num_network_ssid(); i++) {
             net_ssid = dm->get_network_ssid_by_ref(i);
--- a/src/dm/dm_sta_list.cpp
+++ b/src/dm/dm_sta_list.cpp
@@ -246,6 +246,10 @@
 
         case dm_orch_type_db_update:
 			psta = get_sta(key);
+            if (psta == NULL) {
+                em_printfout("Skipping update for absent STA row %s", key);
+                break;
+            }
             memcpy(&psta->m_sta_info, &sta.m_sta_info, sizeof(em_sta_info_t));
             break;

